## Development
{{if .Frontend}}
Frontend (`{{.FrontendPath}}`):

```sh
cd {{.FrontendPath}}
npm ci
npm run lint
npm test --if-present
npm run build
```
{{end}}{{if .Backend}}
Backend (`{{.BackendPath}}`):

```sh
cd {{.BackendPath}}
./mvnw --batch-mode test
./mvnw --batch-mode -DskipTests package
```
{{end}}{{if .Python}}
Python (`{{.PythonPath}}`):

```sh
cd {{.PythonPath}}
uv sync --locked
uv run python -m compileall .
uv run main.py
```
{{end}}
Run `forge validate --path .` from the repository root after changing generated engineering files.

## CI and containers

CI workflows use component path filters, so documentation-only changes do not rebuild applications. Merge requests and pull requests test and build selected components.
{{if .Docker}}Container builds do not publish from review or feature-branch pipelines. Authorized default-branch pushes publish images tagged with the immutable commit SHA.
{{if .Backend}}
The backend image consumes the JAR already produced by Maven. Build it locally after packaging:

```sh
cd {{.BackendPath}}
./mvnw --batch-mode -DskipTests package
docker build -t {{.Project}}-backend .
```
{{end}}{{end}}
See `AGENTS.md` for ownership boundaries.

Preserved directories under `docs/`, `scripts/`, and `deploy/` are available for project-specific material.
